An interesting process can be observed in the Slovene transl ations of three
religious terms: sept (a place of cult), septon (a clergyman of the Faith of
the Seven) and septa (clergyman of the Faith of the Seven). Bo ˇstjan Gorenc
decided to change the word formation of all the words, and sept gained the
feminine gender by the addition of the typical ending -a (septa), whereas
